# Kept in the repo, kept out of the runtime image.
#
# Everything listed here is referenced by no page on the site, but it is not
# junk — most of it is the provenance for what does ship (see
# assets/images/products/CREDITS.md). It stays in git; it just has no reason
# to sit in the deployed image, where the repo root doubles as the public
# document root and main.go's denyBuildFiles only guards the build files at
# the top level, not anything under assets/.
#
# BEWARE the two near-identical directory names:
#   assets/images/products/   SHIPS  — the product photos the site renders
#   assets/img/products/      excluded — the full-size originals those
#                                       photos were cropped from
# Excluding the wrong one silently blanks every product card.

# Full-size originals behind the shipped product crops.
assets/img/products/

# Internal working files: the brand source PDF and the untrimmed logo.
# These would otherwise be fetchable at a guessable URL once deployed.
assets/source/

# Superseded stand-in photography from before the real product shoot.
assets/img/rice.jpg
assets/img/wheat.jpg

# Never needed to build or run the image.
.git
.gitignore
.claude
